WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.054
Part four point one.

2
00:00:01.359 --> 00:00:03.540
A network with a loop in it, and why its

3
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.366
training signal fades with distance.

4
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.095
Lesson three point four called the hidden

5
00:00:11.095 --> 00:00:12.997
state a vector the model carries forward,

6
00:00:12.997 --> 00:00:13.947
a summary of the past.

7
00:00:14.207 --> 00:00:16.022
Here is the simplest machine that does it.

8
00:00:16.281 --> 00:00:17.966
At each slot, one step reads the new

9
00:00:17.966 --> 00:00:19.998
input, x t, and gives out a new state, h

10
00:00:19.998 --> 00:00:20.084
t.

11
00:00:20.343 --> 00:00:22.245
Then that state is fed back in, so at the

12
00:00:22.245 --> 00:00:23.887
next slot the step reads its own last

13
00:00:23.887 --> 00:00:25.270
answer as well as the new input.

14
00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:26.999
That loop is what makes a network

15
00:00:26.999 --> 00:00:27.431
recurrent.

16
00:00:27.829 --> 00:00:29.029
Inside the step is one line.

17
00:00:29.286 --> 00:00:30.530
Build it from the middle out.

18
00:00:30.787 --> 00:00:33.016
First, what it hears: the input x t, times

19
00:00:33.016 --> 00:00:33.488
a weight W.

20
00:00:33.745 --> 00:00:35.846
Plus what it remembers: the last state, h

21
00:00:35.846 --> 00:00:37.947
t minus one, times a second weight, U, the

22
00:00:37.947 --> 00:00:38.847
weight on the memory.

23
00:00:39.104 --> 00:00:40.562
Plus a bias, b, a fixed nudge.

24
00:00:40.819 --> 00:00:42.620
Then tanh squashes the sum into minus one

25
00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.292
to one, as in lesson three point one.

26
00:00:44.549 --> 00:00:46.221
And the result is the new state, h t.

27
00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.229
The weights are the same at every slot.

28
00:00:48.477 --> 00:00:50.217
The step is one machine, used again and

29
00:00:50.217 --> 00:00:50.466
again.

30
00:00:50.714 --> 00:00:52.496
With our five guitar inputs and a state of

31
00:00:52.496 --> 00:00:54.153
a hundred and twenty-eight numbers, W

32
00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.768
would be a hundred and twenty-eight by

33
00:00:55.768 --> 00:00:57.550
five and U a hundred and twenty-eight by a

34
00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:58.585
hundred and twenty-eight.

35
00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:00.532
Our code has no plain recurrent net like

36
00:01:00.532 --> 00:01:02.396
this one; it runs the LSTM of part four

37
00:01:02.396 --> 00:01:04.095
point two, which grew out of this idea.

38
00:01:07.473 --> 00:01:09.705
Draw the loop once for every slot and it

39
00:01:09.705 --> 00:01:12.155
becomes a chain: the state passes along

40
00:01:12.155 --> 00:01:14.550
from left to right, and each slot's input

41
00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:15.639
comes in from below.

42
00:01:15.965 --> 00:01:18.143
Every link uses the same U, and every

43
00:01:18.143 --> 00:01:19.068
input the same W.

44
00:01:19.395 --> 00:01:21.572
Drawing it this way is called unrolling.

45
00:01:21.899 --> 00:01:24.294
Nothing new is computed; it's the same

46
00:01:24.294 --> 00:01:25.655
loop, laid out in time.

47
00:01:25.982 --> 00:01:28.322
To see numbers, shrink everything to one

48
00:01:28.322 --> 00:01:30.990
number: W one and a half, U one half, b

49
00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.004
zero, to keep the arithmetic clean.

50
00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.617
And let the guitar play once, then rest.

51
00:01:36.068 --> 00:01:38.562
Slot one: W times x is one and a half

52
00:01:38.562 --> 00:01:41.346
times one; U times the old state is a half

53
00:01:41.346 --> 00:01:42.912
times zero; plus zero.

54
00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.639
That's one point five, and tanh of one

55
00:01:45.639 --> 00:01:47.959
point five is zero point nine zero five

56
00:01:47.959 --> 00:01:50.395
one, the number from lesson three point

57
00:01:50.395 --> 00:01:50.627
one.

58
00:01:50.975 --> 00:01:53.875
Slot two: the guitar is silent, so W times

59
00:01:53.875 --> 00:01:54.455
x is zero.

60
00:01:54.803 --> 00:01:57.413
All that's left is memory: a half times

61
00:01:57.413 --> 00:01:59.965
zero point nine zero five one, zero point

62
00:01:59.965 --> 00:02:02.343
four five two six, and tanh of that is

63
00:02:02.343 --> 00:02:03.794
zero point four two four.

64
00:02:04.142 --> 00:02:07.042
Slots three, four and five: zero point two

65
00:02:07.042 --> 00:02:09.710
zero nine, zero point one zero four, zero

66
00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:10.870
point zero five two.

67
00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.821
The memory of that one onset about halves

68
00:02:13.821 --> 00:02:15.757
every slot, because U is a half.

69
00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:18.206
This net forgets even going forwards.

70
00:02:18.547 --> 00:02:20.882
In training, lesson three point four's

71
00:02:20.882 --> 00:02:23.273
chunks unroll this chain five hundred and

72
00:02:23.273 --> 00:02:24.298
twelve slots long.

73
00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.717
Lesson three point three: the gradient is

74
00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:32.886
found by the chain rule, one factor for

75
00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:33.712
every step back.

76
00:02:34.022 --> 00:02:36.139
Lesson three point four did this along a

77
00:02:36.139 --> 00:02:38.411
chain of states: backprop through time.

78
00:02:38.721 --> 00:02:40.373
So go backwards along the chain.

79
00:02:40.683 --> 00:02:42.749
To pass from h two back to h one, the

80
00:02:42.749 --> 00:02:44.866
gradient is multiplied by how much h two

81
00:02:44.866 --> 00:02:46.260
changes when h one changes.

82
00:02:46.669 --> 00:02:47.906
Differentiate the step.

83
00:02:48.229 --> 00:02:49.573
The answer has two parts.

84
00:02:49.896 --> 00:02:52.316
The memory weight U, because h j minus one

85
00:02:52.316 --> 00:02:53.607
came in multiplied by U.

86
00:02:53.929 --> 00:02:56.081
Times the slope of tanh at that slot,

87
00:02:56.081 --> 00:02:57.049
written tanh dash.

88
00:02:57.371 --> 00:02:59.738
That slope is one minus h squared: one

89
00:02:59.738 --> 00:03:01.942
where the curve is steepest, near zero

90
00:03:01.942 --> 00:03:02.857
where it is flat.

91
00:03:03.329 --> 00:03:06.178
For slot two: a half times one minus zero

92
00:03:06.178 --> 00:03:08.724
point four two four squared, zero point

93
00:03:08.724 --> 00:03:09.816
four one zero one.

94
00:03:10.179 --> 00:03:12.847
The same at each link: zero point four

95
00:03:12.847 --> 00:03:15.332
seven eight, zero point four nine four

96
00:03:15.332 --> 00:03:17.636
six, zero point four nine eight six.

97
00:03:18.123 --> 00:03:20.290
Four links back, from h five to h one,

98
00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:22.558
multiply all four: zero point zero four

99
00:03:22.558 --> 00:03:22.861
eight.

100
00:03:23.163 --> 00:03:25.229
Under a twentieth of the signal survives

101
00:03:25.229 --> 00:03:25.784
four slots.

102
00:03:26.086 --> 00:03:28.152
And where tanh is squashed flat, it is

103
00:03:28.152 --> 00:03:28.455
worse.

104
00:03:28.757 --> 00:03:30.924
One step further back, through the onset

105
00:03:30.924 --> 00:03:33.192
slot itself, where z was one and a half,

106
00:03:33.192 --> 00:03:35.259
the slope of tanh is only zero point one

107
00:03:35.259 --> 00:03:35.561
eight.

108
00:03:38.907 --> 00:03:40.171
Why does it fall so fast?

109
00:03:40.474 --> 00:03:42.902
Because every factor has the same U in it:

110
00:03:42.902 --> 00:03:44.317
the loop reuses its weights.

111
00:03:44.621 --> 00:03:46.593
A stack of different layers multiplies

112
00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.565
different slopes; a recurrent net

113
00:03:48.565 --> 00:03:50.638
multiplies the same kind of factor again

114
00:03:50.638 --> 00:03:51.144
and again.

115
00:03:51.448 --> 00:03:53.521
Say every factor is the same number, a.

116
00:03:53.824 --> 00:03:55.999
Then n slots back the gradient is a to the

117
00:03:55.999 --> 00:03:56.403
power n.

118
00:03:56.858 --> 00:03:59.492
With a equal to a half, like our toy: a

119
00:03:59.492 --> 00:04:01.847
half one slot back, zero point zero six

120
00:04:01.847 --> 00:04:04.257
two five four back, fifteen millionths a

121
00:04:04.257 --> 00:04:06.723
bar back, and five times ten to the minus

122
00:04:06.723 --> 00:04:08.012
twenty after four bars.

123
00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:09.974
The far past teaches nothing.

124
00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.992
That's the vanishing gradient.

125
00:04:12.474 --> 00:04:14.672
With a equal to one and a half, it goes

126
00:04:14.672 --> 00:04:17.185
the other way: six hundred and fifty-seven

127
00:04:17.185 --> 00:04:19.383
a bar back, two times ten to the eleven

128
00:04:19.383 --> 00:04:20.220
after four bars.

129
00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:22.576
One step of training would be enormous.

130
00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.460
That's the exploding gradient.

131
00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:27.187
Lesson three point three's clipping is the

132
00:04:27.187 --> 00:04:29.526
patch for exploding: a gradient longer

133
00:04:29.526 --> 00:04:31.545
than one is scaled down to length one.

134
00:04:31.864 --> 00:04:33.725
But clipping only ever scales down.

135
00:04:34.044 --> 00:04:36.276
It can't make a vanishing gradient bigger.

136
00:04:36.595 --> 00:04:39.359
Our LSTM, L32, never needed it: it clipped

137
00:04:39.359 --> 00:04:40.954
on none of its training steps.

138
00:04:41.273 --> 00:04:43.558
With a hundred and twenty-eight numbers in

139
00:04:43.558 --> 00:04:45.791
the state, each factor is a hundred and

140
00:04:45.791 --> 00:04:48.076
twenty-eight by a hundred and twenty-eight

141
00:04:48.076 --> 00:04:50.255
matrix rather than one number, but the

142
00:04:50.255 --> 00:04:52.807
rule is the same: what matters is how much

143
00:04:52.807 --> 00:04:54.082
it stretches or shrinks.

144
00:04:57.407 --> 00:04:58.315
Now the real thing.

145
00:04:58.602 --> 00:05:00.849
Take our LSTM, L32 at epoch eleven, at the

146
00:05:00.849 --> 00:05:03.143
worked slot: validation song zero zero one

147
00:05:03.143 --> 00:05:05.103
one b three c f, slot five hundred and

148
00:05:05.103 --> 00:05:06.777
seventy-six, the downbeat of bar

149
00:05:06.777 --> 00:05:07.302
thirty-six.

150
00:05:07.589 --> 00:05:09.501
Ask how much its kick logit there moves

151
00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:11.509
when the guitar inputs at an earlier slot

152
00:05:11.509 --> 00:05:13.374
move: the length of that gradient.

153
00:05:13.661 --> 00:05:15.716
The axis is a log axis, as in lesson one

154
00:05:15.716 --> 00:05:17.867
point four: each step down is ten times

155
00:05:17.867 --> 00:05:18.250
smaller.

156
00:05:18.665 --> 00:05:20.994
One slot back, where the guitar played an

157
00:05:20.994 --> 00:05:22.899
onset: zero point two one five.

158
00:05:23.217 --> 00:05:25.228
Four back, zero point zero five two.

159
00:05:25.545 --> 00:05:27.980
Sixteen back, one bar: zero point zero

160
00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:28.668
zero two one.

161
00:05:28.986 --> 00:05:31.421
Sixty-four back, four bars: zero point

162
00:05:31.421 --> 00:05:32.797
zero zero zero four eight.

163
00:05:33.114 --> 00:05:35.655
Five hundred and twelve back: twenty-three

164
00:05:35.655 --> 00:05:36.237
millionths.

165
00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.098
Against the slot just heard, the gradient

166
00:05:39.098 --> 00:05:41.537
falls about a hundred times within a bar,

167
00:05:41.537 --> 00:05:43.920
about four hundred and fifty times by four

168
00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:46.358
bars, and about nine thousand six hundred

169
00:05:46.358 --> 00:05:48.520
times by five hundred and twelve slots.

170
00:05:48.852 --> 00:05:51.235
At this slot, the kick barely depends on

171
00:05:51.235 --> 00:05:52.787
guitar more than a bar back.

172
00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:55.336
This is one logit's gradient, not the

173
00:05:55.336 --> 00:05:57.497
training loss, which covers all nine

174
00:05:57.497 --> 00:06:00.268
drums; but it is a fair proxy, because the

175
00:06:00.268 --> 00:06:02.596
training gradient passes back through the

176
00:06:02.596 --> 00:06:04.147
same chain of state factors.

177
00:06:04.579 --> 00:06:06.299
Training cut it shorter still.

178
00:06:06.643 --> 00:06:09.050
This is a validation song, so L32 never

179
00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.687
trained on it; but L32 trained in chunks

180
00:06:11.687 --> 00:06:14.267
of five hundred and twelve, with the state

181
00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:16.846
detached at every chunk edge, lesson three

182
00:06:16.846 --> 00:06:18.910
point four, and the edges fall at

183
00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.030
multiples of five hundred and twelve.

184
00:06:21.374 --> 00:06:23.839
Had this been a training song, slot five

185
00:06:23.839 --> 00:06:25.788
hundred and seventy-six would sit

186
00:06:25.788 --> 00:06:28.024
sixty-four slots past the edge at five

187
00:06:28.024 --> 00:06:30.546
hundred and twelve, so its gradient would

188
00:06:30.546 --> 00:06:33.010
