189
00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.615
beyond that, exactly zero.

190
00:06:36.011 --> 00:06:36.979
One honest point.

191
00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.597
L32 isn't the plain loop of this lesson.

192
00:06:39.939 --> 00:06:42.329
It's an LSTM, which already has the fix

193
00:06:42.329 --> 00:06:44.208
that part four point two teaches.

194
00:06:44.549 --> 00:06:46.655
And its gradient still falls about a

195
00:06:46.655 --> 00:06:48.192
hundred times within a bar.

196
00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:51.095
So the fix helps; it doesn't remove the

197
00:06:51.095 --> 00:06:51.607
fall-off.

198
00:06:51.949 --> 00:06:54.112
Part four point two shows why most of

199
00:06:54.112 --> 00:06:55.819
L32's cells still forget fast.

200
00:06:56.161 --> 00:06:58.608
And all of this is one slot of one song,

201
00:06:58.608 --> 00:06:59.633
at one checkpoint.

202
00:06:59.974 --> 00:07:02.308
A fact check at four other slots of this

203
00:07:02.308 --> 00:07:04.983
song found the same direction: falls of a

204
00:07:04.983 --> 00:07:07.260
hundred and twenty to two hundred times

205
00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.000
within a bar.

206
00:07:09.576 --> 00:07:12.103
Say it in one breath: a recurrent net

207
00:07:12.103 --> 00:07:14.336
feeds its last state back in at every

208
00:07:14.336 --> 00:07:16.863
slot, h equals tanh of W x plus U h plus

209
00:07:16.863 --> 00:07:16.980
b.

210
00:07:17.333 --> 00:07:19.684
Going back, every slot multiplies the

211
00:07:19.684 --> 00:07:22.269
gradient by U times the slope of tanh, so

212
00:07:22.269 --> 00:07:24.737
it shrinks geometrically, the vanishing

213
00:07:24.737 --> 00:07:27.206
gradient, or grows, the exploding one.

214
00:07:27.558 --> 00:07:30.085
Measured on our LSTM at the worked slot,

215
00:07:30.085 --> 00:07:32.436
it falls about a hundred times within a

216
00:07:32.436 --> 00:07:32.671
bar.

